GLib already skips installing the gdb auto-load scripts when the target
system is Windows, because the install path embeds the library directory
and a Windows drive letter contains a colon.  When GLib is cross-built
*on* Windows for a Linux target (as in the HiSH OHOS build), the target
system is not Windows but the install path still contains "D:/..." and
Meson's installer fails with WinError 123 after all libraries have been
installed.

Also skip the gdb auto-load scripts when the build machine is Windows.
The scripts are debugging helpers and are not used by QEMU.

--- a/glib/meson.build
+++ b/glib/meson.build
@@ -528,11 +528,11 @@
 gdb_conf = configuration_data()
 gdb_conf.set('datadir', glib_datadir)
 # This is also used in gobject/meson.build
-if host_system != 'windows'
+if host_system != 'windows' and build_machine.system() != 'windows'
   gdb_install = true
 else
-  # FIXME: Cannot install on Windows because the path will contain a drive
-  # letter and colons are not allowed in paths.
+  # FIXME: Cannot install on Windows (host or build machine) because the path
+  # will contain a drive letter and colons are not allowed in paths.
   gdb_install = false
 endif
 
